          "owner_id": "own_925824",
          "prev_trainers": [],
          "prev_owners": [],
          "comment": "",
          "spotlight": "",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-05-20",
              "horse": "Ciara Pearl",
              "horse_id": "hrs_36416506",
              "race": "Dine In Sherwoods Restaurant Fillies' Handicap (Jockey Club Middle Distance Qualifier) (GBBPlus)",
              "race_id": "rac_11619491",
              "course": "Nottingham",
              "course_id": "crs_1040",
              "distance_f": "10",
              "distance_y": "2250",
              "quote": "Ciara Pearl ran in a Listed race last week and probably only had to run to that level. She settled well, caught a breather round the bend and we're rolling on three furlongs out. She's very adaptable, fast ground or slow. They've [joint-trainers Daniel and Claire Kubler] done a remarkable job with her - Jim Crowley, jockey, speaking to Racing TV."
            },
            {
              "date": "2024-10-25",
              "horse": "Ciara Pearl",
              "horse_id": "hrs_36416506",
              "race": "Renegade Brewery Fillies' Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_11412440",
              "course": "Newbury",
              "course_id": "crs_936",
              "distance_f": "10",
              "distance_y": "2200",
              "quote": "You never know with the ground until they've run. Ciara Pearl has won on soft, but not that sort of ground. She had a chance and I didn't think the first two would pull that far clear of the rest of the field - Daniel Kubler, joint-trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2023-10-05",
              "horse": "Ciara Pearl",
              "horse_id": "hrs_36416506",
              "race": "Sky Sports Racing Sky 415 Restricted Novice Stakes (For Horses In Bands C And D) (GBB Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11034998",
              "course": "Lingfield (AW)",
              "course_id": "crs_10218",
              "distance_f": "8",
              "distance_y": "1761",
              "quote": "Ciara Pearl was very green first time out at Bath and speaking to Cieren (Fallon) this morning, who rode her, he said the mile would probably be her minimum trip at the minute. Around that top bend we were getting slower and slower but she's just got one big stride and that's why I wheeled out and let her use her stride down the hill and she stayed on strongly - Jack Mitchell, jockey, speaking on Sky Sports Racing."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "She's done nothing but progress and ran really well the other day at Chelmsford. She's won seven of her 20 starts. A mile is probably a bit sharp for her, but she does stay and if they got a lot of rain then it could give her an outside squeak. She's been far from disgraced twice in Listed races and handles any going. 10-06-25"
            },
            {
              "quote": "She's done nothing but progress and she ran really well the other day at Chelmsford. She's won seven of her 20 starts and she'll go to Royal Ascot for the Kensington Palace. A mile is probably a bit sharp for her, but she does stay and if they got a lot of rain it could give her an outside squeak. If she can run her race then we'll mix and match between some of the valuable fillies' handicaps this season. We hope she can get some black type, which would make her a good prospect as a broodmare. She's been far from disgraced twice in Listed races and she handles any going. 11-06-25"
            }
          ],
