              "course_id": "crs_416",
              "distance_f": "8",
              "distance_y": "1762",
              "quote": "Zowal had shown good form in France last year, he's pleased us since we've had him and that was a really nice start. He was just rolling around a little bit. Hopefully he'll improve going forward and still learn. When we first got him we thought he might be a mile-and-a-quarter horse and wouldn't have been stunned if he was a mile-and-a-half horse, but he's not shy of speed. He'd been working at home with Empirestateofmind, who ran in the Spring Mile, so that convinced us to start at a mile and take it from there - Sean Quinn, joint-trainer, speaking on Racing TV."
