          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2022-09-11",
              "horse": "Streets Of Gold",
              "horse_id": "hrs_30850449",
              "race": "Tattersalls Ireland Super Auction Sale Stakes",
              "race_id": "rac_10640058",
              "course": "Curragh",
              "course_id": "crs_4628",
              "distance_f": "6.5",
              "distance_y": "1383",
              "quote": "Charlie (Bishop, rider) said Streets Of Gold hated the ground and never really went a yard in it, but I thought he was always going to get there. You wouldn't know he was in the yard. He just doesn't work well at home, he never has, so it's hard to know what you've got - Eve Johnson Houghton, trainer"
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "This bonny lad is a real superstar. He only made his debut 12 months ago but by the middle of October had won five times from as many starts including a valuable nursery at York and a big sales race at the Curragh. It was a great run of success for his owners and he earned over £234,000. He has never stopped improving and although he has not won this year he has run cracking races each time. After finding the heavy ground too much for him in the Greenham we had his breathing operated on and he has put up two career-best efforts since. At Epsom he was third in Listed company and last time out at Royal Ascot he was third again, this time in the Group 3 Jersey Stakes, which was a cracking run. He may go to Newmarket this week for the Bunbury Cup, which historically has not been a good race for 3yos, but I think you will find not too many of that age group attempt the race. He seems in great form and I am sure there are more nice races to be won with him. 11-07-23"
            }
          ],
