          "comment": "",
          "spotlight": "",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-04-20",
              "horse": "Electric Storm",
              "horse_id": "hrs_36484987",
              "race": "Whitsbury Manor Stud / British EBF Lansdown Stakes (Listed Race) (Fillies & Mares)",
              "race_id": "rac_11575499",
              "course": "Bath",
              "course_id": "crs_130",
              "distance_f": "5",
              "distance_y": "1110",
              "quote": "We kept Electric Storm in training hoping she'd improve and it looks like it's possible. She's won two Listed races on extremely quick ground and another on very heavy, so she's definitely versatile. We'll look at Group races with her now. There's a Group 3 in France in three weeks [the Prix de Saint-Georges at Longchamp] or the Temple Stakes at Haydock. We'll look at one of those and see if we can do better than last year - James Tate, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2024-05-24",
              "horse": "Electric Storm",
              "horse_id": "hrs_36484987",
              "race": "EBF British Stallion Studs Cecil Frail (Listed Race) (Fillies & Mares)",
              "race_id": "rac_11267932",
              "course": "Haydock",
              "course_id": "crs_598",
              "distance_f": "6",
              "distance_y": "1320",
              "quote": "Electric Storm had some developmental issues as a yearling so really she didn't train as a two-year-old and only stepped up her training midsummer as a three-year-old. She's got the speed for five but she stays seven, I think six is probably her ideal trip. I think there will be further improvement there. We have three four-year-old fillies by Night Of Thunder - Cloud Cover won on All-Weather Finals day, Royal Dress won a Listed race at Goodwood a couple of weeks ago and now this filly has won a Listed race too - James Tate, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2023-08-16",
              "horse": "Electric Storm",
              "horse_id": "hrs_36484987",
              "race": "Unibet/Breeders Backing Racing EBF Fillies' Novice Stakes (GBB Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_10999326",
              "course": "Kempton (AW)",
              "course_id": "crs_28054",
              "distance_f": "7",
              "distance_y": "1540",
              "quote": "Electric Storm is a sweet little thing but she was very green and didn't like the kickback. I loved her attitude inside the last 150yds, she really put her neck down to the floor for me, and she's definitely something for connections to look forward to - Ray Dawson, jockey, talking to RacingTV."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "She started the year off well and broke the track record at Bath in a fillies' and mares' Listed race - the form was really good too. Then, as can happen with sprinters, she hasn't had the rub of the green since. She had a bad draw and missed the kick in France and then was a creditable fourth in the Temple. She was probably on the wrong side there, although there was nothing wrong with that performance - Mgheera won it well on the favoured stands' rail and we had the Group 1 winner American Affair just behind us. Then at Ayr last time the front-runner went far too fast and we chased it and ended up bursting her slightly, but again she wasn't beaten far. I'm sure her turn is coming around again. She's going to go for the Group 3 Summer Stakes on Friday at York, which is a quick 6f. She's been running over 5f recently but we thought maybe that Ayr showed she doesn't want as quick a 5f as that. She has worked great at home and we'll be going into the race with confidence. 09-07-25"
            }
          ],
