          "sire_id": "sir_4989285",
          "sire_region": "IRE",
          "damsire": "Bob's Return",
          "damsire_id": "dsi_510566",
          "damsire_region": "IRE",
          "trainer": "Paul John Gilligan",
          "trainer_id": "trn_117756",
          "trainer_location": "Athenry, Co Galway",
          "trainer_14_days": {
            "runs": "6",
            "wins": "1",
            "percent": "17"
          },
          "owner": "E Lynch & T C Quinn & John J McGrath",
          "owner_id": "own_1294744",
          "prev_trainers": [],
          "prev_owners": [],
          "comment": "",
          "spotlight": "",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2024-10-08",
              "horse": "Buddy One",
              "horse_id": "hrs_32668405",
              "race": "Guinness Chase",
              "race_id": "rac_11421553",
              "course": "Galway",
              "course_id": "crs_4758",
              "distance_f": "22.5",
              "distance_y": "4951",
              "quote": "Buddy One jumped great, he was clever and shortened when he had to. Where we go from here, I don't know, but obviously our main aim is to try to get back to Cheltenham. He'll definitely face stiffer opposition through the winter, but that was a lovely experience for him - Paul John Gilligan, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2024-04-13",
              "horse": "Buddy One",
              "horse_id": "hrs_32668405",
              "race": "JRL Group Liverpool Hurdle (Grade 1) (GBB Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11221691",
              "course": "Aintree",
              "course_id": "crs_832",
              "distance_f": "24.5",
              "distance_y": "5429",
              "quote": "It would have been nice to win it but we're happy. Buddy One is a fantastic horse. Is he going to win a Grade 1 over hurdles? He hasn't yet but he's on the premises the whole time. He's entered at Punchestown but I'd imagine that's it. He won at Cheltenham in November and he has been boxing in the main arena since and has been boxing with credit - Paul Gilligan, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2024-03-14",
              "horse": "Buddy One",
              "horse_id": "hrs_32668405",
              "race": "Paddy Power Stayers' Hurdle (Grade 1) (GBB Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11124295",
              "course": "Cheltenham",
              "course_id": "crs_286",
              "distance_f": "24",
              "distance_y": "5273",
              "quote": "It was an absolutely super run. If the ground was just a touch better it would have suited Buddy One better, but I'm not complaining. I won't go to Punchestown, but I think he might go to Aintree as he ran very well there last year. I will talk to his owners to see what we do - Paul Gilligan, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2023-11-18",
              "horse": "Buddy One",
              "horse_id": "hrs_32668405",
              "race": "Paddy Power Games Handicap Hurdle (GBB Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11075168",
              "course": "Cheltenham",
              "course_id": "crs_286",
              "distance_f": "24",
              "distance_y": "5268",
              "quote": "I didn't think Buddy One would be beaten today, his Galway run last time was really good. He was winning this race today off top-weight, he has gone out of handicaps now. Depending how he comes out of today he'll go for the Hatton's Grace - you meet Willie [Mullins] and Gordon [Elliott] wherever you go, but this is so special - Paul Gilligan, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2023-10-28",
              "horse": "Buddy One",
              "horse_id": "hrs_32668405",
              "race": "W.B. Gavin & Co. Handicap Hurdle",
              "race_id": "rac_11086699",
              "course": "Galway",
              "course_id": "crs_4758",
              "distance_f": "22",
              "distance_y": "4820",
              "quote": "Buddy One deserved to win that. He's been consistent always, he has carried a big weight and won as he liked. We would hope to kick on now to Cheltenham in November. He is going the right way - Paul Gilligan, trainer"
            }
          ],
